# Trivy ignore file — reviewed, documented exceptions only.
#
# Each entry MUST carry a reason. These are accepted *portfolio* trade-offs that
# are already explained in ARCHITECTURE.md (§4, §12). TIGHTEN these for prod.
#
# VERIFIED 2026-10-17, and two of the three do not fire:
#
#   AVD-AWS-0054  fires (CRITICAL). This suppression does real work.
#   AVD-AWS-0040  does not fire.
#   AVD-AWS-0041  does not fire.
#
# Not because the risk went away — because Trivy does not read tfvars, and
# `endpoint_public_access = true` with `public_access_cidrs = ["0.0.0.0/0"]` lives
# in environments/<env>/terraform.tfvars. The scan sees `var.public_access_cidrs`
# and cannot resolve it, so the finding never appears and the suppression is never
# needed.
#
# They are kept rather than deleted precisely because of that: the posture they
# describe is real and the scanner is blind to it. Deleting them would leave the
# repository looking clean on a risk nobody withdrew. If `--tf-vars` is ever added
# to the scan, expect both to start firing and to be doing real work again.
#
# How to verify locally:
#   trivy config --severity HIGH,CRITICAL .

# EKS public API endpoint is intentionally enabled so Terraform can run from
# GitHub-hosted runners (no in-VPC self-hosted runners). Gated by
# public_access_cidrs. See ARCHITECTURE.md §4. Tighten public_access_cidrs in
# prod; revisit moving to a private-only endpoint.
AVD-AWS-0040

# public_access_cidrs defaults to 0.0.0.0/0 for hml/demo. This is the documented
# portfolio default; prod MUST narrow it to office/CI egress ranges
# (ARCHITECTURE.md §10, §12). Remove this exception once prod restricts the CIDR.
AVD-AWS-0041

# The platform ingress listener serves plain HTTP. The load balancer is
# `internal = true` and its security group admits only the VPC CIDR, so the
# unencrypted hop exists entirely inside the VPC — there is no eavesdropping
# position on the public internet to defend against yet.
#
# Terminating TLS here needs an ACM certificate, which needs a delegated domain.
# That is `enable-external-app-access`, and this change deliberately keeps to one
# axis (ARCHITECTURE.md §3, §12). This exception MUST be removed in that change:
# the listener gains a certificate and port 80 becomes a redirect. If external
# access lands and this line is still here, the platform is serving plaintext to
# the internet.
AVD-AWS-0054
